Promote consumer-readable Decision Case results UX.

This release applies the agreed consumer-facing design rule: what have we found -> why does it matter -> what should I do.

Changes:
- replace 'Decision-critical evidence is still missing' with 'Important information is still missing';
- remove the unexplained '8 unresolved evidence items remain' style count and replace it with plain-English context;
- remove duplicate 'Next:' and 'Do this:' instructions;
- provide one clear Next step and one primary action: Send questions to installer;
- increase heading, body and question text sizes and spacing for desktop/mobile readability;
- retain the balanced two-panel results layout;
- improve Quote evidence completeness and Quote Facts typography without changing the underlying analysis;
- preserve free comparison and the personalised £19 Decision Pack boundary.

